      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. The GCD is the largest number that divides both numbers without leaving a remainder. Using the Euclidean algorithm, we can compute the GCD of 342 and 285:\n\n1. Divide 342 by 285: \\(342 = 285 \\cdot 1 + 57\\). So, \\(342 = 285 \\cdot 1 + 57\\).\n2. Divide 285 by 57: \\(285 = 57 \\cdot 5 + 0\\). So, \\(285 = 57 \\cdot 5\\).\n\nThe remainder in the Euclidean algorithm is zero, and the last non-zero remainder is the GCD. In this case, the GCD of 342 and 285 is 57.\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
